// @@@ If the index is valid (between 0 and the size of the list minus one), then for every position greater than the index up to the end of the list, the element at that position either remains unchanged or continues to be null if it was initially null.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is valid (non-negative and less than the size of the list), then for every position greater than the index up to the end of the list, either both the current and old values at that position are null, or the current value at that position equals the old value at that position.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is valid (non-negative and less than the size of the list), then for every position i greater than the index and less than the size of the list, either both the current and old values at position i are null, or the current value at position i equals the old value at position i.
--------------------
